The bus is very crowded.
I find a seat near the window.
I sit down.
I am looking out the window.
There are many cars on the road.
The morning traffic is moving forward slowly.
The conductor comes near me.
He is asking everyone for tickets.
"Madam, ticket," he says to me.
I open my bag.
I take out the money.
"One ticket, Dada," I say politely.
I give him twenty rupees.
He gives me a small ticket.
He gives me five rupees back.
"Thank you," I say.
I put the ticket in the bag.
I look out the window again.
My bus is going towards the office.
